1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,800
 Hi, in this lesson, I will talk about the main problems of prompt engineering.

2
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:06,320
 Let's get started.

3
00:00:06,320 --> 00:00:09,640
 Let's talk about main problems in prompt engineering.

4
00:00:09,640 --> 00:00:13,840
 AI models learn from massive datasets collected online.

5
00:00:13,840 --> 00:00:20,640
 Unfortunately, these datasets often contain unfair patterns or stereotypes.

6
00:00:20,640 --> 00:00:27,320
 When we write prompts, the AI may repeat the same biases or even make them stronger.

7
00:00:27,320 --> 00:00:30,640
 This can result in unfair or offensive outputs.

8
00:00:30,640 --> 00:00:35,760
 That's why prompt engineers must always watch for bias and actively work to reduce it.

9
00:00:35,760 --> 00:00:38,200
 Human language is not always clear.

10
00:00:38,200 --> 00:00:42,880
 A single word of phrase can carry several different meanings.

11
00:00:42,880 --> 00:00:49,560
 For example, the word Java would mean a programming language or it could mean an island.

12
00:00:49,560 --> 00:00:54,440
 This makes it challenging to write prompts that are both clear enough for the AI to understand

13
00:00:54,440 --> 00:00:57,560
 and flexible enough to allow for creative answers.

14
00:00:57,560 --> 00:01:03,320
 Sometimes, AI produces wrong information, which is also called hallucinations.

15
00:01:03,320 --> 00:01:10,000
 It may also change its style of tone when asked similar questions, which feels inconsistent.

16
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:15,440
 This inconsistency makes it hard to trust the results, especially for important tasks

17
00:01:15,440 --> 00:01:17,600
 like coding of finance.

18
00:01:17,600 --> 00:01:23,760
 If a prompt contains too many details, the response can feel robotic or overly narrow.

19
00:01:23,760 --> 00:01:31,400
 On the other hand, if the prompt is to open, the AI might produce random or off-topic answers.

20
00:01:31,400 --> 00:01:36,640
 Prompt engineers must find the right balance between guiding the AI and leaving enough room

21
00:01:36,640 --> 00:01:39,040
 for fresh and creative ideas.

22
00:01:39,040 --> 00:01:42,920
 Some tasks are very complex and involve many steps.

23
00:01:42,920 --> 00:01:48,440
 For example, analyzing data, creating insights, and then writing a report.

24
00:01:48,440 --> 00:01:53,480
 Breaking these big tasks into smaller steps is not always easy, and the AI may skip

25
00:01:53,480 --> 00:01:58,120
 parts or become confused, let's switch now into technical problems.

26
00:01:58,120 --> 00:02:04,840
 AI models cannot always remember long conversations, and they may forget earlier parts

27
00:02:04,840 --> 00:02:07,960
 or misunderstand what the user meant.

28
00:02:07,960 --> 00:02:13,960
 Even with well-designed prompts, this can lead to incomplete or irrelevant answers, AI tools

29
00:02:13,960 --> 00:02:19,560
 are changing rapidly, new models are released often, and older ones may behave differently

30
00:02:19,560 --> 00:02:22,240
 after updates.

31
00:02:22,240 --> 00:02:29,040
 This means that a prompt that worked well last week may not work the same way today.

32
00:02:29,040 --> 00:02:33,440
 Prompt engineers must skip learning and adjusting as models evolve.

33
00:02:33,440 --> 00:02:38,240
 It is not always clear why the AI gives a certain response.

34
00:02:38,240 --> 00:02:42,480
 Unlike normal code, prompts function more like a black box.

35
00:02:42,480 --> 00:02:47,520
 This makes it difficult to debug and improve prompt step by step.

36
00:02:47,520 --> 00:02:52,600
 Prompt engineering usually requires a lot of testing and fixing.

37
00:02:52,600 --> 00:02:58,320
 Pandings is processed for a single case may be fine, but doing it across many projects

38
00:02:58,320 --> 00:03:01,960
 or large teams becomes very difficult to manage.

39
00:03:01,960 --> 00:03:05,160
 Finally, let me introduce to you user problems.

40
00:03:05,160 --> 00:03:09,720
 Many users simply do not know how to write effective prompts.

41
00:03:09,720 --> 00:03:14,240
 And this often leads to wasted time, poor answers, and frustration.

42
00:03:14,240 --> 00:03:18,600
 That's why clear training is needed to help people use AI in the right way.

43
00:03:18,600 --> 00:03:22,560
 Poorly written prompts can also create serious risks.

44
00:03:22,560 --> 00:03:28,880
 For example, users might accidentally share private or sensitive data.

45
00:03:28,880 --> 00:03:35,280
 But prompts can also help malicious actors create harmful content or lead the AI to generate

46
00:03:35,280 --> 00:03:39,080
 unsafe or unethical outputs.

47
00:03:39,080 --> 00:03:43,360
 Prompt engineers must always skip safety and security in mind.

48
00:03:43,360 --> 00:03:48,080
 And summary prompt engineering is powerful, but it is not easy.

49
00:03:48,080 --> 00:03:54,040
 The main problems include bias, unclear language, incorrect, or unstable outputs, finding

50
00:03:54,040 --> 00:03:59,840
 the right balance between details and creativity and handling complex tasks.

51
00:03:59,840 --> 00:04:05,040
 There are also technical issues such as remembering contacts, adapting to fast-changing

52
00:04:05,040 --> 00:04:08,600
 models, and scaling up work effectively.

53
00:04:08,600 --> 00:04:14,560
 Finally, users need proper training to avoid mistakes and reduce risks.

54
00:04:14,560 --> 00:04:18,800
 I hope this lesson was useful for you and see you in the next lesson.

